    "created_at": "2016-10-19T16:17:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-19T16:17:47Z",
    "body": "The spec parser uses a bunch of heuristics to infer dfn types from legacy specs, in this case the quotes around the 'px' are causing the bare &lt;dfn> to be interpreted as a value, which does get auto-exported. Removing the heuristic will break a bunch of other specs, best solution is to either add a data-noexport or a data-dfn-type='dfn' (to force the dfn's to not get auto-typed) to a containing element (it'll propagate to all contained dfn's that don't override).\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
