    "created_at": "2016-10-19T23:33:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-19T23:33:39Z",
    "body": "Sure, sorry I didn't mean to imply that Bikeshed is doing this. Shepherd spec parser has heuristics _similar_ to Bikeshed's auto-detection, which are based on content found in legacy specs (like CSS2.1).\n\nI agree these shouldn't be definitions. Using a `data-lt=\"\"` will prevent them from being linked to by Bikeshed (and maybe ReSpec), but Shepherd will still see them as definitions, and still infer that they are CSS values. Adding a `data-dfn-type='dfn'` will force them to not be detected as values by Shepherd, adding a `data-noexport` will prevent them from being exported, or simply not using the &lt;dfn> tag will prevent them from being seen as definitions in the first place (which is arguably more correct because you're not defining these terms in the HTML spec, you're linking to the definitions).\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
